{
	"note": "World spaces and coordinates (roadmap item 41; core/game/game_spaces.gd, checked by tools/check_data.gd). Every place the game has is a space with an id of its own and a position, so the text game's map and the sandbox name places the same way. Ids are paths: `world` is the open world (the generated surface and the ground under it); a town or a stretch of wilds is an AREA of it, `world/hearthmere`, a region round the place's anchor tile that is walked into; a dungeon is an INTERIOR, `world/goblin_warrens`, a space of its own entered through a door on the open world; a town's services are interiors of the town, `world/hearthmere/forge`, each with its door a few tiles from the town's centre (`service_doors`, as [east, south] of it, inside the town's cleared ground); and the family house is an interior of the home town (`house`). `kind_of_type` says which kind each place type in world.json is. UNDERWORLD: `underworld` gives the shaft, a tile of the open world where the ground goes down, and the mining zones (data/mining/mining.json) that are bands of it, each a space `world/underworld/<zone>`: the first is entered from the open world at the shaft, each deeper one from the band above it, all at the shaft's own tile, and a band's depth runs from its zone's first cell to the next zone's. REALMS: `realm_gates` gives the tile of the open world where each realm's gate stands (not the home realm, which has none); every realm in data/creatures/realms.json is a space `realm/<id>`, a child of the open world at its gate, and the home realm is listed with no door since the open world is its ground. ROOMS: `rooms` gives each interior's floor plan, keyed by the layout it uses (a service's name, a dungeon's place id, or the house's id). A layout is a list of rooms (`id`, `name`, `rect` [x, z, width, height] in tiles on the interior's own floor, x east and z south, origin at the door, which must lie in the one `entrance` room) and `doors` ({from, to, at}: `at` is the gap tile between two rooms that touch it). Nothing here is saved or random: a space is worked out from world.json, this file, mining.json, realms.json and GameWorldGen's anchors. TOWN DOORS: `town_doors` gives, for each town, the door tile of each shop of data/shops/shops.json ([east, south] of the town's anchor, inside its cleared ground); the six old services keep one door in `service_doors` for every town.",
